\title{RSEncoding Protocol}
\description{
The \code{RSEncoding} protocol defines the requirements for any object that supports
structural encoding via the \code{RSClassEncoder} with \code{RSEncodingProtocol} and
\code{RSClassDecoder} with \code{RSDecodingProtocol}. Conforming classes must explicitly
declare which child objects should be recursively encoded, and must support
class substitution during decoding.

This protocol is implemented by all robjc classes that need to be serialized.
It requires the presence of two methods: \code{objectsForEncoding()} and
\code{resolveClassWith(new_cls)}.
}
\details{
\itemize{
\item \code{objectsForEncoding()}: Returns a list of robjc objects to be encoded
along with the object itself.
\item \code{resolveClassWith(new_cls)}: Called during decoding to replace the object's
class reference (\code{.__isa}) with the actual runtime class.
}
}
